# activity/puzzledb/.env — the puzzle database site's settings (db.tetrisatuci.org).
# Copy to puzzledb/.env and set DATABASE_PATH. Nothing in this file is secret.
#
# Its own file, never activity/.env. The site is started from activity/ as
#   bun --env-file=puzzledb/.env puzzledb/server/main.ts     (or: bun run puzzledb)
# and --env-file *replaces* Bun's usual .env loading, so the game's secrets never
# enter this process. Without it, Bun reads the .env of the directory it starts in,
# which from activity/ is the game's: the site then finds the game's secrets in its
# environment and refuses to start, naming the variable and never its value.
#
# Bun skips an --env-file it cannot find without a word and runs on. That is why
# DATABASE_PATH has no default: a mistyped path to this file leaves it unset, and the
# site stops and says so rather than opening a database it guessed.

# ── The game's database ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Required. The absolute path of the game's own daily.sqlite: the file the running
# game writes, never a copy or a backup. If activity/.env sets DATABASE_PATH, use the
# same file, written absolute; if it does not, the game uses
# <checkout>/activity/data/daily.sqlite. A relative path is refused.
#
# Opened read-only. A path with nothing at it is reported and retried, never created.
# Run the site as the OS user the game runs as: even a read-only reader can create
# the -wal and -shm files beside the database, and the site warns at start-up when
# the file belongs to somebody else.
DATABASE_PATH=

# ── Daily rotation ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Must match the game's DAILY_RESET_TIMEZONE, because it decides which days are over
# and may be shown. Like the game, it defaults to America/Los_Angeles when unset
# (DEFAULT_TIME_ZONE in shared/daily.ts). A zone that is not a known IANA name stops
# the site at start-up with the game's own message.
#DAILY_RESET_TIMEZONE=America/Los_Angeles

# ── Server ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The loopback port: the site listens on 127.0.0.1 only. Its own name, because an
# inherited variable beats this file, and a shell or pm2 environment set up for the
# game can carry PORT=3001; the site never reads PORT. Whole digits from 0 to 65535;
# 0 takes any free port.
PUZZLEDB_PORT=3002

# No TRUST_PROXY here, on purpose: every peer a loopback listener sees is the proxy
# on this box, so the site always counts callers by Cf-Connecting-Ip, then the last
# X-Forwarded-For entry, and the proxy must overwrite both (puzzledb/DEPLOY.md).
